## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate a feature into a practical 12‑month CBA with edge constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference costs (latency, energy, memory)
- Privacy and data minimization
- Cloud review costs vs offline results
- Rollout strategy and drift/maintenance costs
- Break-even horizon selection

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateCBA(modelSizeMB, perInferenceJ, inferencesPerMonth, cloudCostPerEvent) {
  const energyKJ = perInferenceJ * inferencesPerMonth;
  const yearlyEnergyCost = (energyKJ / 1000) * 0.9;
  const cloudYear = cloudCostPerEvent * inferencesPerMonth * 12;
  const total = modelSizeMB + yearlyEnergyCost + cloudYear;
  return total;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify drift/maintenance costs and retraining cadence?
- How would latency targets influence model size vs accuracy trade-offs?
- What metrics would you track to decide go/no-go?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to translate a complex edge-ML rollout into a precise 2-year CBA, balancing hardware, cloud costs, and real-world benefits like downtime and maintenance savings.

## Key Concepts

- Edge computing and on-device training
- Federated learning and privacy implications
- CAPEX vs OPEX modeling
- Downtime reduction and MTBF uplift as financial drivers
- Handling non-IID data and drift in multi-site deployments

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateROI(capex, opexPerMonth, savingsPerMonth, horizonMonths) {
  const totalOpex = opexPerMonth * horizonMonths;
  const totalCost = capex + totalOpex;
  const totalSavings = savingsPerMonth * horizonMonths;
  const roi = (totalSavings - totalCost) / totalCost;
  return { totalCost, totalSavings, roi };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor and mitigate model drift across sites?
- What metrics would you track to validate the ROI assumptions and trigger governance gates?

